      "category": "code",
      "visible_expectation": "BitsToBytes updates byte B[floor(i/8)] using b[i]*2^(i mod8), then returns B; preserve code step order and exponent.",
      "expected_behavior": "preserve_figure_separation",
      "layer_status": "not-applicable",
      "detector_expected": false,
      "outline_expected": null,
      "related_locations": [],
      "review_basis": "source image + native layer only",
      "native_clip": "Algorithm 3 BitsToBytes(𝑏) \nConverts a bit array (of a length that is a multiple of eight) into an array of bytes. \nInput: bit array 𝑏 ∈ {0,1}8⋅ℓ . \nOutput: byte array 𝐵 ∈ 𝔹ℓ . \n1: 𝐵 ← (0,…,0) \n2: for (𝑖 ← 0; 𝑖 < 8ℓ; 𝑖++) \n3: \n𝐵[⌊𝑖/8⌋] ← 𝐵[⌊𝑖/8⌋]+𝑏[𝑖]⋅2𝑖 mod 8 \n4: end for \n5: return 𝐵"
    },
